    summary: 'Heaven’s Gate was an American UFO new religious movement founded in 1975 by Marshall Applewhite ("Do") and Bonnie Nettles ("Ti"). Synthesizing Christian apocalyptic scripture with science fiction tropes, the group believed their physical bodies were mere "vehicles" (containers) for souls preparing to graduate to the "Next Level" (the Kingdom of Heaven). On March 26, 1997, 39 members were discovered deceased inside a rented mansion in Rancho Santa Fe, California, having ingested phenobarbital and vodka in the belief that an extraterrestrial spacecraft trailing Comet Hale-Bopp would transport them to an extraterrestrial existence.',
