    summary: 'The Church Committee was the United States Senate Select Committee to Study Governmental Operations with Respect to Intelligence Activities, chaired by Idaho Democratic Senator Frank Church in 1975–1976. Established in the aftermath of the Watergate scandal and Seymour Hersh’s New York Times exposé of illegal domestic CIA spying, the committee conducted the first comprehensive public investigation into the covert operations, assassination plots, biological weapons stockpiles, and unconstitutional domestic surveillance conducted by the CIA, FBI, NSA, and military intelligence.',
