    counterEvidence: 'The Church Committee operated with strict bipartisan integrity, holding 126 public hearings, interviewing over 800 witnesses, and reviewing over 110,000 classified documents. The committee’s findings led directly to landmark structural reforms: the permanent establishment of the Senate Select Committee on Intelligence (SSCI) and House Permanent Select Committee on Intelligence (HPSCI), President Gerald Ford’s Executive Order 11905 banning political assassinations, and the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (FISA) of 1978 requiring judicial warrants for foreign intelligence surveillance within the US.',
