    summary: 'United States mass surveillance comprises a vast architecture of domestic and international signals intelligence collection operated by the National Security Agency (NSA) under legislative authorizations including Section 702 of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (FISA) and Section 215 of the USA PATRIOT Act. Tracing roots back to Cold War programs like Project SHAMROCK (1945–1975), the modern dragnet was dramatically expanded post-9/11 under the secret Stellar Wind program. In June 2013, NSA contractor Edward Snowden leaked thousands of top-secret documents to journalists Glenn Greenwald and Laura Poitras, exposing programs including PRISM, XKeyscore, and bulk domestic telephony metadata collection.',
