    counterEvidence: 'Official declassified reports from the Privacy and Civil Liberties Oversight Board (PCLOB) in 2014 and 2020 confirmed that while the NSA did not routinely record full audio content of all domestic calls, the bulk metadata program collected billions of phone records without individual reasonable suspicion and yielded minimal unique counterterrorism benefits. In 2015, Congress enacted the USA FREEDOM Act, officially terminating bulk telephone metadata storage by the NSA and requiring telephone carriers to retain records subject to individual FISC queries.',
